# SKE Starter Kit

✅ **Your environment is ready!**

This starter kit has set up the following resources in workspace `${workspace_identifier}`:

@buildingblock[${git_repository_uuid}]
%{ for stage in stages ~}

@project[${stage.project_workspace}.${stage.project_name}]\
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@tenant[${stage.tenant_uuid}]\
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;@buildingblock[${stage.forgejo_connector_uuid}]
%{ endfor ~}

---

## What's Included

Your [Forgejo repository](${repo_html_url}) on STACKIT Git was initialized from `${repo_clone_addr}`.
Its Forgejo Actions pipeline builds the `${app_name}` image and deploys it to the SKE namespace of each stage.

Each stage's Forgejo Connector wired the repository to that stage's namespace with the Actions
secrets and variables `KUBECONFIG_<STAGE>`, `K8S_NAMESPACE_<STAGE>` and `APP_HOSTNAME_<STAGE>`.

---

## Deployments

Each stage deploys from the branch of the same name. The Forgejo Connector already ran the
`pipeline.yaml` workflow once per stage, so your app is live:

%{ for stage in stages ~}
- **${title(stage.name)}**: [${stage.app_hostname}](https://${stage.app_hostname})
%{ endfor ~}

View deployment status: [Forgejo Actions](${repo_html_url}/actions?workflow=pipeline.yaml)

---

## Next Steps

### 1. Develop
%{ for stage in stages ~}
- Push changes to **${stage.name}** → deploys to **${stage.name}**
%{ endfor ~}

### 2. Monitor
- Check workflow status in the [Actions tab](<${repo_html_url}/actions>)

### 3. Manage Access
- Invite team members via meshStack:
%{ for stage in stages ~}
  - [${title(stage.name)} Access](#/w/${workspace_identifier}/p/${stage.project_name}/access-management/role-mapping)
%{ endfor ~}

---

🎉 Happy coding!
